 {2}^{2x-6}+3\\cdot {2}^{2x-6} & =0 \\\\ (8{x}^{2}-10x+3)\\cdot {2}^{2x-6} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n8{x}^{2}-10x+3=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{2}^{2x-6}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $8{x}^{2}-10x+3=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(2x-1)(4x-3)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{3}{4}.$\n\n- The equation ${2}^{2x-6}=0$ has no solutions because ${2}^{2x-6}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the original equation has the solutions \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{and}\\,x=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186517453 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186517467 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186517453 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186517453 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the product of solutions of the equation ${x}^{2}{9}^{5-x}=81\\cdot {9}^{5-x}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186517453 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7e99061e-44c6-52dd-9617-5709b63b42f7" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186517453 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}{9}^{5-x} & =81\\cdot {9}^{5-x} \\\\ {x}^{2}{9}^{5-x}-81\\cdot {9}^{5-x} & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-81){9}^{5-x} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-81=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{9}^{5-x}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation ${x}^{2}-81=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(x+9)(x-9)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-9,9.$\n\n- The equation ${9}^{5-x}=0$ has no solutions because ${9}^{5-x}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, the original equation has the solutions $x=-9,9,$ and their product is $(-9)\\cdot 9=-81.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186517462 #edb/ref 10